<title>INDIA: INDIA COALITION OIL PRICE HIKE MEETING AT 5.00 P.M.</title>
<headline>INDIA COALITION OIL PRICE HIKE MEETING AT 5.00 P.M.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The decision-making steering committee of India's ruling United Front is scheduled to hold a meeting at 5.00 p.m. (1130 GMT) on Wednesday to discuss a possible increase in oil prices, a coaltion official said.</p>
<p>The committee is expected to consider hikes in the prices of diesel and liquefied petroleum gas (LPG) to lower a deficit of 190 billion rupees ($5.3 billion) owed by the government to state owned firms for selling their products below the market prices.</p>
<p>Communist parties have led opposition within the United Front to any hike in the price of diesel or kerosene, which they say could stoke inflation or hurt the poor.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi Newsroom (91) 11-301-2024; Fax (91) 11-301-4043</p>
